<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers harvested 4.2 percent of their 1996/97 sunflower crop by Feb 7, Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>But humidity in south Buenos Aires was providing a good breeding ground for sunflower fungus, especially esclerotinia. Maize was being attacked in some areas by Rio Cuarto virus, which stunts growth. Attacks have been worst in west Buenos Aires, south Santa Fe and southwest Cordoba. But it is hard to calculate the effect on output, especially as the number of plants sown per hectare was higher than last season.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,782   99.3(100.0)    33.5    0.9   (0.4)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,412   99.7(100.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,039  100.0(100.0)   124.7    4.2   (2.0)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     777   99.0 (98.7)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	964  100.0  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
